It also ports parts of CPython (https://www.python.org), Copyright (c) 2001-2024
Python Software Foundation; All Rights Reserved. Summary of the changes: the regular
expression parser (Lib/re/_parser.py, with the checks of Lib/re/_compiler.py) is
translated to Rust and, instead of compiling patterns for CPython's engine, translates
them for the fancy-regex crate; str repr (Objects/unicodeobject.c), pprint and textwrap
formatting (Lib/pprint.py, Lib/textwrap.py) and str.format field parsing
(Objects/stringlib/unicode_format.h) are translated to Rust and work on JSON values only.
